        "notes[1].title": "Microsoft Teams API Integration",
        "notes[2].content": "This functional block manages the overall workflow execution flow and response processing from the webinar registration API.\n\n**Purpose**: Control workflow execution logic and handle the response from the Microsoft Teams API registration call.\n\n**Execution Control**:\n- **Transition Mode**: FOLLOW_ALL - ensures all connected tasks execute\n- **Join Strategy**: Standard join (0) for single-task execution\n- **Timeout**: 600-second maximum execution time for the task\n- **Retry Policy**: Standard retry handling for transient failures\n\n**Success Path Handling**:\n- **Condition**: {{ SUCCEEDED }} - triggers when API call completes successfully\n- **Next Task ID**: ${UUID} (currently no follow-up tasks configured)\n- **Response Processing**: API response available for downstream tasks or workflow output\n\n**Workflow State Management**:\n- Task enabled for execution\n- No mocking configured (runs against live API)\n- No custom organization context override\n- Standard error propagation behavior\n\n**Integration Points**:\n- **Input Source**: Receives customer data from workflow context variables\n- **Output Destination**: API response available for potential follow-up tasks\n- **Error Handling**: Standard workflow error handling applies\n\n**Future Extension Points**:\n- Success/failure notification tasks can be added to the next task chain\n- Response data can be processed for confirmation emails or logging\n- Additional validation or retry logic can be inserted before API call\n\n**Current State**: Single-task workflow focused on webinar registration with room for expansion based on business requirements.",
